1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,846
Every January,

2
00:00:00,846 --> 00:00:02,055
millions of capable,

3
00:00:02,055 --> 00:00:05,681
well-paid people promise themselves that this year they will

4
00:00:05,681 --> 00:00:08,521
rely on stricter discipline to save more money.

5
00:00:08,521 --> 00:00:09,065
By March,

6
00:00:09,065 --> 00:00:10,093
unexpected bills,

7
00:00:10,093 --> 00:00:11,301
stressful Thursdays,

8
00:00:11,301 --> 00:00:14,565
and one-click checkout buttons quietly erase the plan.

9
00:00:14,565 --> 00:00:18,312
Traditional budgeting fails because it asks an exhausted brain

10
00:00:18,312 --> 00:00:19,037
at nine P.M.

11
00:00:19,037 --> 00:00:22,965
to win three hundred and sixty-five consecutive willpower battles

12
00:00:22,965 --> 00:00:23,509
in a row.

13
00:00:23,509 --> 00:00:27,015
Yet in a landmark 2004 Journal of Political Economy study,

14
00:00:27,015 --> 00:00:31,366
behavioral economists Richard Thaler and Shlomo Benartzi watched average

15
00:00:31,366 --> 00:00:36,503
employee retirement savings climb from three-point-five percent to thirteen-point-six

16
00:00:36,503 --> 00:00:38,981
percent without lecturing anyone on grit.

17
00:00:38,981 --> 00:00:41,640
They replaced willpower with pre-commitment.

18
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:44,411
Decades before modern fintech apps existed,

19
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:48,857
Nobel Prize-winning economist Thomas Schelling studied the paradox of

20
00:00:48,857 --> 00:00:52,594
self-command in his classic essays Choice and Consequence.

21
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:55,301
Schelling pointed back to Homer's Odyssey:

22
00:00:55,301 --> 00:00:58,651
Odysseus knew that once he heard the Sirens singing,

23
00:00:58,651 --> 00:01:01,422
his future self would beg to steer the ship

24
00:01:01,422 --> 00:01:02,389
onto the rocks.

25
00:01:02,389 --> 00:01:04,580
So while the water was still calm,

26
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:07,995
he stuffed his sailors' ears with beeswax and ordered

27
00:01:07,995 --> 00:01:10,379
them to lash him tightly to the mast.

28
00:01:10,379 --> 00:01:15,019
Schelling showed that every household contains two competing characters:

29
00:01:15,019 --> 00:01:18,692
a patient Tuesday morning planner and an impulsive Friday

30
00:01:18,692 --> 00:01:19,594
night spender.

31
00:01:19,594 --> 00:01:22,880
Pre-commitment hands the steering wheel to Tuesday.

32
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,325
Economists Nava Ashraf,

33
00:01:24,325 --> 00:01:25,078
Dean Karlan,

34
00:01:25,078 --> 00:01:28,407
and Wesley Yin put Schelling's Ulysses Pact through a

35
00:01:28,407 --> 00:01:31,171
rigorous real-world test in the Philippines,

36
00:01:31,171 --> 00:01:35,504
publishing their findings in the 2006 Quarterly Journal of Economics.

37
00:01:35,504 --> 00:01:37,326
Partnering with a rural bank,

38
00:01:37,326 --> 00:01:41,848
they offered randomly selected clients a commitment account called SEED.

39
00:01:41,848 --> 00:01:44,486
It paid the exact same interest rate as an

40
00:01:44,486 --> 00:01:45,993
ordinary liquid account,

41
00:01:45,993 --> 00:01:46,935
with one catch:

42
00:01:46,935 --> 00:01:51,080
savers voluntarily locked their own withdrawals until they reached

43
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:53,844
either a chosen goal date or target balance.

44
00:01:53,844 --> 00:01:55,100
Twelve months later,

45
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:58,931
average savings balances across the group offered SEED jumped

46
00:01:58,931 --> 00:02:02,009
eighty-one percent higher than the control group.

47
00:02:02,009 --> 00:02:04,270
Friction protected their intentions.

48
00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:08,771
Thaler and Benartzi's Save More Tomorrow architecture took pre-commitment

49
00:02:08,771 --> 00:02:12,285
even further by aligning three human quirks that normally

50
00:02:12,285 --> 00:02:13,272
sabotage wealth.

51
00:02:13,272 --> 00:02:15,923
When you ask workers to cut spending out of

52
00:02:15,923 --> 00:02:17,341
next Friday's paycheck,

53
00:02:17,341 --> 00:02:20,917
present bias and loss aversion rebel immediately because a

54
00:02:20,917 --> 00:02:23,692
smaller deposit feels like a painful pay cut.

55
00:02:23,692 --> 00:02:24,185
Instead,

56
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:27,576
Thaler and Benartzi invited employees to sign up months

57
00:02:27,576 --> 00:02:30,228
in advance to route a slice of their future

58
00:02:30,228 --> 00:02:32,879
annual pay raises straight into retirement.

59
00:02:32,879 --> 00:02:35,469
Because today's paycheck stayed untouched,

60
00:02:35,469 --> 00:02:37,010
signing up felt painless.

61
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:38,551
Whenever a raise arrived,

62
00:02:38,551 --> 00:02:40,894
net take-home pay still rose slightly,

63
00:02:40,894 --> 00:02:46,074
while status-quo inertia carried savings from three-point-five to thirteen-point-six

64
00:02:46,074 --> 00:02:47,800
percent across forty months.

65
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:51,464
Compare those two experiments with how most people organize

66
00:02:51,464 --> 00:02:53,203
their digital banking today.

67
00:02:53,203 --> 00:02:57,613
Trillion-dollar retail platforms employ thousands of engineers to shave

68
00:02:57,613 --> 00:02:59,724
half a second off mobile checkout:

69
00:02:59,724 --> 00:03:00,469
saved cards,

70
00:03:00,469 --> 00:03:01,649
biometric face-pay,

71
00:03:01,649 --> 00:03:03,575
and buy-now buttons everywhere.

72
00:03:03,575 --> 00:03:06,866
If your emergency reserve and freedom fund sit inside

73
00:03:06,866 --> 00:03:09,723
the exact same banking app as your debit card,

74
00:03:09,723 --> 00:03:11,897
one tap away from instant transfer,

75
00:03:11,897 --> 00:03:14,257
you have built a reverse Ulysses Pact.

76
00:03:14,257 --> 00:03:19,349
Protecting wealth in a frictionless consumer economy requires asymmetric friction:

77
00:03:19,349 --> 00:03:22,952
zero effort for dollars flowing into compounding accounts,

78
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:26,802
paired with deliberate multi-day speed bumps before any dollar

79
00:03:26,802 --> 00:03:27,920
can come back out.

80
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:32,439
Build your personal pre-commitment architecture tonight using three locks.

81
00:03:32,439 --> 00:03:34,332
Lock One is the External Vault:

82
00:03:34,332 --> 00:03:37,508
open a high-yield reserve and brokerage account at a

83
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:40,989
completely separate institution from your daily checking,

84
00:03:40,989 --> 00:03:42,760
cut up any optional ATM card,

85
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:46,118
and automate payday splits so accessing that cash takes

86
00:03:46,118 --> 00:03:47,950
a three-business-day transfer.

87
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:51,126
Lock Two is your Personal Save-More-Tomorrow Pledge:

88
00:03:51,126 --> 00:03:54,729
write down a standing rule tonight committing fifty percent

89
00:03:54,729 --> 00:03:56,073
of every future raise,

90
00:03:56,073 --> 00:03:56,439
bonus,

91
00:03:56,439 --> 00:04:00,958
or side-business jump directly into long-term investments before lifestyle

92
00:04:00,958 --> 00:04:02,546
creep ever sees the money.

93
00:04:02,546 --> 00:04:05,477
Lock Three is the Seventy-Two-Hour Cooling Rule:

94
00:04:05,477 --> 00:04:08,775
delete saved credit cards from browsers and wait three

95
00:04:08,775 --> 00:04:12,011
days on discretionary buys over one hundred and fifty

96
00:04:12,011 --> 00:04:12,500
dollars.
